title: Suspicious Child Processes of Samsung MagicINFO Tomcat
id: 13492049-498b-4c32-871d-4b973f6cd8ab
status: experimental
description: >
    Detects post-exploitation activity of CVE-2025-4632 against Samsung
    MagicINFO 9 Server: every observed step ran as a child of
    tomcat9.exe — certutil and PowerShell pulling AnyDesk from
    194.87.89.30:8899, and compiler tooling (csc.exe, cvtres.exe,
    tcc.exe, cc1.exe, gcc.exe, donut.exe) building a Monero miner on
    the host — plus explorer.exe launched with RandomX mining
    arguments targeting auto.c3pool.org:19999 (Huntress, September
    2026).
references:
    - https://www.huntress.com/blog/threat-actor-compiles-cryptominer
    - https://www.huntress.com/blog/post-exploitation-activities-observed-from-samsung-magicinfo-9-server-flaw
author: Tia N. List
date: 2026/09/25
tags:
    - attack.t1190
    - attack.t1105
    - attack.t1500
    - attack.t1059
logsource:
    category: process_creation
    product: windows
detection:
    selection_parent:
        ParentImage|endswith: '\tomcat9.exe'
    selection_child:
        Image|endswith:
            - '\certutil.exe'
            - '\powershell.exe'
            - '\anydesk.exe'
            - '\csc.exe'
            - '\cvtres.exe'
            - '\tcc.exe'
            - '\cc1.exe'
            - '\gcc.exe'
            - '\donut.exe'
    selection_miner:
        Image|endswith: '\explorer.exe'
        CommandLine|contains: 'c3pool.org'
    condition: (selection_parent and selection_child) or selection_miner
falsepositives:
    - Legitimate administrative use of certutil, PowerShell or AnyDesk on a MagicINFO host
    - Benign compiler invocations under the MagicINFO Tomcat process during vendor maintenance
level: high
